WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:04.620
Since Russia invaded Ukraine, maps of the
conflict are everywhere.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:07.309
In most cases, shaded areas, like this red

00:00:07.309 --> 00:00:10.740
are meant to symbolize territory occupied
by Russian forces

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.548
or at least, territory Russia and Ukraine
are fighting over.

00:00:14.548 --> 00:00:18.018
In general, this red is referring to 
ground troops, like these.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:21.648
The more the Russian ground troops advance,
the more of the map turns red.

00:00:21.648 --> 00:00:24.275
But what maps like these don’t show 
is another battle

00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:26.574
that’s taking place high above Ukraine. 

00:00:26.574 --> 00:00:30.101
Where a small Ukrainian air force is fighting
a powerful Russian one 

00:00:30.101 --> 00:00:31.872
for control of the skies.

00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:35.199
What happens here could determine not just
the course of the war

00:00:35.199 --> 00:00:38.109
but whether it escalates and spreads 
beyond Ukraine.

00:00:38.851 --> 00:00:41.884
It’s why Ukraine’s allies are scrambling
to send it weapons.

00:00:41.884 --> 00:00:44.030
And some are asking to go a step further:

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:44.736
"No-fly zone."

00:00:44.736 --> 00:00:45.236
"No-fly zone."

00:00:45.236 --> 00:00:46.064
"A no-fly zone."

00:00:46.064 --> 00:00:46.573
[chanting] "No-fly zone!"

00:00:46.573 --> 00:00:47.727
"A humanitarian no-fly zone."

00:00:47.727 --> 00:00:50.149
"No-fly zone seems to make sense."

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:52.700
"Well, I think you that all know 
what I'm going to say."

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.296
"We need the no-fly zone over Ukraine."

00:00:55.296 --> 00:00:58.324
So, why are the stakes of this air war 
so high?

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:01.255
And what would a no-fly zone change?

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:11.238
On February 24, 2022, the Russian invasion
of Ukraine began.

00:01:11.238 --> 00:01:14.439
And in terms of military strategy, it followed
a common script.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:17.255
First, Russian missiles targeted 
Ukraine’s radar system.

00:01:17.255 --> 00:01:20.075
Then its airfields and some missile launchers.

00:01:20.075 --> 00:01:23.734
To military experts, this appeared to be 
preparation for a crucial step.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:26.630
Send a lot of planes to destroy 
the Ukrainian air force

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:29.281
and achieve what’s called “Air Superiority."

00:01:29.281 --> 00:01:32.009
So when we say a military has air superiority

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:36.785
what we're essentially saying is a military
more or less controls the skies.

00:01:36.785 --> 00:01:40.579
With air superiority, Russia could freely
attack Ukrainian ground troops

00:01:40.579 --> 00:01:42.006
and protect its own ground troops

00:01:42.006 --> 00:01:45.332
who could move faster without fear
of being attacked from the skies.

00:01:45.332 --> 00:01:50.380
If Russia were able to establish virtually
unchallenged air superiority

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:52.149
it would be a disaster for Ukraine.

00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:54.261
Doesn't mean you're guaranteed a victory 

00:01:54.261 --> 00:01:56.704
but it makes that victory a heck of a lot more likely.

00:01:56.704 --> 00:01:58.378
That's why since World War II

00:01:58.378 --> 00:02:02.095
winning air superiority has been 
the first step in most invasions.

00:02:02.095 --> 00:02:05.105
But in this case, the big attack never came.

00:02:05.105 --> 00:02:07.603
And experts don’t really agree on why.

00:02:07.603 --> 00:02:09.694
My best informed guess is that 

00:02:09.694 --> 00:02:12.913
Russians thought that they would be welcome 
when they got there.

00:02:12.913 --> 00:02:15.700
And so when they saw men, women, and children

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.340
blocking their tanks from entering 
Ukrainian villages

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.390
that surprised them.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:23.310
When you make war plans, including plans related
to air superiority

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.237
if your assumptions are wrong, then your plan
is messed up.

00:02:26.237 --> 00:02:29.530
Whatever happened, it means that, more than
two weeks into the invasion

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.230
Russia did not have total air superiority.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.549
It allowed the Ukrainian air force 
to defend themselves

00:02:34.549 --> 00:02:37.280
against some Russian fighter jets 
and ground forces

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.868
helping bog down the Russian invasion.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:43.951
This was celebrated as part of Ukraine’s
remarkable resistance early on in the war.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.753
It's a function of both Ukrainian success
and also some surprising 

00:02:49.753 --> 00:02:52.864
shortcomings in Russian military capability.

00:02:52.864 --> 00:02:55.445
But it might not last much longer.

00:02:55.445 --> 00:03:00.260
When you compare the Russian military and
the Ukrainian military there is no comparison.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.890
In every major metric of power, the Russian
military is far more powerful

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.890
including when it comes to aviation.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:11.700
Russia has more than ten times the number
of fighter aircraft as Ukraine.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.037
And so far, they haven’t really used them.

00:03:14.037 --> 00:03:18.530
It's possible over the coming days and weeks
that Putin and his military leaders decide

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:21.811
to make greater use of Russian aircraft.

00:03:21.811 --> 00:03:24.422
And I think that's already happening.

00:03:24.422 --> 00:03:28.325
They're entering a new phase where, in my
view, they're systematically

00:03:28.325 --> 00:03:30.319
using air power in part

00:03:30.319 --> 00:03:33.762
to systematically attack civilians and civilian
infrastructure.

00:03:33.762 --> 00:03:36.458
That means the Russians still 
could win air superiority

00:03:36.458 --> 00:03:40.670
which would help speed up their invasion,
and likely cause significant civilian casualties.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:44.406
So, Ukraine’s allies are frantically trying
to keep that from happening.

00:03:44.406 --> 00:03:46.056
Many countries are sending weapons 

00:03:46.056 --> 00:03:49.689
that Ukrainian ground troops can use 
to shoot down Russian aircraft.

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:53.121
And there have been talks about 
sending Ukraine planes.

00:03:53.121 --> 00:03:58.021
But there’s also been talk of 
another kind of help: a no-fly zone.

00:03:58.021 --> 00:04:02.576
Ukrainian president Volodmyrr Zelenskyy has
asked NATO, the western military alliance,

00:04:02.576 --> 00:04:04.465
to declare a no-fly zone.

00:04:04.465 --> 00:04:08.335
A number of US foreign policy experts 
have called for a limited no-fly zone

00:04:08.335 --> 00:04:13.180
and a recent poll shows 74% of Americans 
think the US should declare one.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.123
So, what is a No-Fly Zone?

00:04:16.123 --> 00:04:21.620
Basically it’s a geographic area, where
certain plains are prohibited from flying.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:24.259
The point of NATO declaring 
a No-Fly Zone over Ukraine

00:04:24.259 --> 00:04:27.204
would be to prevent Russia from 
winning air superiority

00:04:27.204 --> 00:04:29.788
thereby protecting Ukraine’s 
military and civilians.

00:04:29.788 --> 00:04:33.970
But what makes a no-fly zone complicated 
is how NATO would have to enforce it.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.733
To propose the no-fly zone in Ukraine

00:04:36.733 --> 00:04:40.209
if you're going to be serious about it,
you have to consider that to enforce it 

00:04:40.209 --> 00:04:41.419
to make it a real thing

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:44.848
you would actually have to shoot down 
Russian aircraft.

00:04:44.848 --> 00:04:48.175
This means NATO would be directly 
participating in the conflict

00:04:48.175 --> 00:04:51.752
escalating the war to involve 
the US and most of Europe.

00:04:51.752 --> 00:04:54.627
The establishment of a no-fly zone 
sooner or later 

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:57.518
puts us in a high risk of direct combat.

00:04:57.518 --> 00:05:02.114
And don't for a minute think that 
you can control how that escalates.

00:05:02.114 --> 00:05:06.023
Once one aircraft gets shot down, 
whether it's ours or theirs

00:05:06.023 --> 00:05:08.445
all bets are off on what happens next.

00:05:08.445 --> 00:05:12.620
Russia is a nuclear armed power and Putin's
been making a lot of threats to suggest that

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.479
he thinks nuclear weapons might be an option.

00:05:15.479 --> 00:05:17.960
All this would also be true of a 
"limited no-fly zone"

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:21.808
which would only cover certain areas, but
would be enforced in the same way.

00:05:21.808 --> 00:05:26.070
Putin has vowed to treat anyone imposing a
no-fly zone as a “participant in the conflict”.

00:05:26.658 --> 00:05:30.710
And, so far, president Biden and NATO leaders
have ruled it out.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:33.608
So for now, even while its allies send weapons

00:05:33.608 --> 00:05:36.774
Ukraine will have to do the fighting themselves.

00:05:36.774 --> 00:05:39.101
Every bone in my body wants to help Ukrainians.

00:05:39.101 --> 00:05:42.944
They're fighting for all of us, and I weep
when I see some of these images.

00:05:42.944 --> 00:05:46.779
But I think we should do all that we can 
to help Ukraine

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:51.105
while also doing everything we can to avoid
direct conflict with Russia.

